<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.5.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00449</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.5.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>99fcba6d-00a9-4640-a4c4-e7a8a6547d5d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<para>For questions 1 – 4, add the equations in the system to find a new equation.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="c03daac5-e19e-4214-9ed3-81dd1107a242"><problem><para>
      <para> \( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} 6x - 5y = -1\\ -6x - 3y = -39 \end{array}\right. \)</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(2y = –38\)</para><para>\(–2y = –40\)</para><para>\(–8y = –40\)</para><para>\(–8x = –40\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(–8y = –40\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(–8y = –40\).
      </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section>
<para>For questions 5 – 10, solve each system of equations.</para>

<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="1cc9948d-650a-4ef9-b839-056b65aa9185"><problem><para>
      <para>
          \( \left\{ \begin{array}{c l} 6x + 27y = -12\\ -6x - 26y = 14 \end{array}\right. \)</para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((2.5,–1)\)</para><para>\((–11,2)\)</para><para>\((7,–1)\)</para><para>\((–20,4)\)</para></problem><solution><para>\((–11,2)\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \((–11,2)\).
      </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
